    proof: "A^T A is symmetric and positive semidefinite, so it has a spectral factorization V D V^T with nonnegative eigenvalues σᵢ². Let vᵢ be the columns of V and set σᵢ = √(the corresponding eigenvalue). For each σᵢ > 0 define uᵢ = A vᵢ / σᵢ. Then ⟨uᵢ, uⱼ⟩ = ⟨A vᵢ, A vⱼ⟩ / (σᵢ σⱼ) = ⟨A^T A vᵢ, vⱼ⟩ / (σᵢ σⱼ) = σᵢ / σⱼ · δᵢⱼ, so the uᵢ are orthonormal. Extend them to an orthonormal basis of the codomain, the remaining columns of U. By construction A vᵢ = σᵢ uᵢ for the positive singular values and A vᵢ = 0 for the rest, which is the matrix equation A V = U Σ. Multiply on the right by V^T.",
